{"event_type":"review","id":"5a7ce9c4b32c45fe7382de588e83648b4fbf1313b647d5a224bf4eb87f2a7ea8","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T13:39:59Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6a1a8341cba9bb912e1ad4bcee8cec351e3b0ca77e470b89ad50ab414cd2ebe6","sha256":"6a1a8341cba9bb912e1ad4bcee8cec351e3b0ca77e470b89ad50ab414cd2ebe6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/35471d46d7f33fed8bcbf690d2ffb71ffc66356a1174862ab5295cac9f3d2852","sha256":"35471d46d7f33fed8bcbf690d2ffb71ffc66356a1174862ab5295cac9f3d2852"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/32a1acf36d07479a07763b6b3e6469dca4e2e7377dc78e9d086ddcf1ae8b2669","sha256":"32a1acf36d07479a07763b6b3e6469dca4e2e7377dc78e9d086ddcf1ae8b2669"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/519bbde1ba6a00fde397716ef5e59bb8faee22ff15ec4bba975d71c077aa938f","sha256":"519bbde1ba6a00fde397716ef5e59bb8faee22ff15ec4bba975d71c077aa938f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/00decfe943541dfbb9e7daedd0bf18a44500ff1fbd12508f95f5aefd7a95fd48","sha256":"00decfe943541dfbb9e7daedd0bf18a44500ff1fbd12508f95f5aefd7a95fd48"}],"attempt_id":"43e74ea810af542a080b756d2705a8e8743d3caa4455a7b88b70b33e6eea0081:0:1","base":"d1b6ebf4523f23653a60a5405e2c802a8de16e3a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"001cf54c9f9d27b3fceacb71ba87c663c036993a","body":"**Reject non-regular files in `readWorktreeFile`.**\n\nAfter the symlink check, the code accepts any entry type. `lstat` reports `size` 0 for a FIFO, so the `capBytes` check passes. `readFile` at Line 273 then blocks forever, because a FIFO read never reaches EOF without a writer. One such entry in the worktree hangs the whole secret scan. The scan has no timeout, and this effect is documented as fail-closed.\n\nRefuse anything that is not a regular file, with the cause named.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         if (stats.isSymbolicLink()) return { ok: false, reason: `symlink (not followed): ${path}` };\n+        if (!stats.isFile()) return { ok: false, reason: `not a regular file: ${path}` };\n```\n</details>\n\nConfirm that the caller's file list comes only from tracked files. If it does, this guard is purely defensive, but the fix is still one line.","id":"c278ca46e3457ab812b437e754efd732ab868882437cefbbc5897f7321c24e60","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/effects.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject non-regular files in `readWorktreeFile`."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"01bec66faf65611b5317a3f0caeb97da06cc8ef0","body":"**Guard registry setup before accessing input.**\n\nIn `src/ops/dev/registry.ts:217-223`, a direct SDK call with `null` rejects before `guardDevOp` can return a `failed` result. An empty `repoRoot` causes reads of `/cq.json` and `/package.json` before validation. The `dev.review` and `dev.cycle` wrappers have the same ordering.\n\nWrap each wrapper’s setup in `guardDevOp` with its matching schema. Preserve the `dev.review` admission branch.","id":"744bc3bdc831078327fa753e46b5e2402202414a77d72447c0aed215a9a5b0ce","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/registry.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Guard registry setup before accessing input."}],"head":"62581528ee88d0cfe3de5259158cbcff07d4d190","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"748094b30e783c9858d95223aaf3c489ae36b820","intervals":[[1,557]],"path":"src/ops/dev/denylist.ts"},{"blob":"001cf54c9f9d27b3fceacb71ba87c663c036993a","intervals":[[1,330]],"path":"src/ops/dev/effects.ts"},{"blob":"01bec66faf65611b5317a3f0caeb97da06cc8ef0","intervals":[[1,440]],"path":"src/ops/dev/registry.ts"}],"job_id":"43e74ea810af542a080b756d2705a8e8743d3caa4455a7b88b70b33e6eea0081:0","outcome":